because this is other really important stuff I have to do. And in that case, I would say that is not procrastinating. He does, he's not putting it off. He doesn't think he should do it now. He very legitimately has simply reordered his priorities to reflect. It's a conscious decision. Yes. And so I think procrastination is in some ways a subjective state. that it depends on the psychology of why people are doing it and how they feel about it. The good news, this is very preliminary, but we do have data that for academic procrastination, at least, that I'm not going to go so far as to say you should do productive procrastination. That's definitely too far.

